  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1930\" data-end=\"2066\">\n<p data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"1949\"><strong data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"1947\">Normal VEP:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1952\" data-end=\"2066\">\n<li data-start=\"1952\" data-end=\"2006\">\n<p data-start=\"1954\" data-end=\"2006\">Symmetrical latencies and amplitudes in both eyes.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2009\" data-end=\"2066\">\n<p data-start=\"2011\" data-end=\"2066\">P100 latency within normal limits (&le;115 ms for adults).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2068\" data-end=\"2281\">\n<p data-start=\"2070\" data-end=\"2089\"><strong data-start=\"2070\" data-end=\"2087\">Abnormal VEP:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2092\" data-end=\"2281\">\n<li data-start=\"2092\" data-end=\"2190\">\n<p data-start=\"2094\" data-end=\"2190\"><strong data-start=\"2094\" data-end=\"2115\">Prolonged latency</strong> (often in <strong data-start=\"2126\" data-end=\"2186\">optic neuritis, demyelination such as multiple sclerosis</strong>).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2193\" data-end=\"2281\">\n<p data-start=\"2195\" data-end=\"2281\"><strong data-start=\"2195\" data-end=\"2216\">Reduced amplitude</strong> or <strong data-start=\"2220\" data-end=\"2233\">asymmetry</strong> between eyes (may indicate conduction defects).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2283\" data-end=\"2349\">\n<p data-start=\"2285\" data-end=\"2349\">Must be interpreted with <strong data-start=\"2310\" data-end=\"2348\">clinical findings and neuroimaging</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
